-- title:
--   At q=2, points reading non-node places avoid supersingular j
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Two function fields inside Laurent series are in play: $\overline{F}_{M'} :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the rational full level-$M'$ modular function field, and $\mathcal{F} :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\overline{F}_{M'} \le \mathcal{F}$.
--
--   Reduction data. $W$ is a finite set of places (in the sense of the project's `Place`: a valuation subring containing the base field, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring) of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\overline{F}_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, a scaling property for nonzero elements, and a place map preserving degrees and pushing forward principal divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\overline{F}_{M'}$ belongs to `R₀.integers`, with $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Branch data. $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `Idx q`), $\mathrm{OIg}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal{F}$ to each point of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $\mathrm{OSS}$ one to each $s \in W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` describes $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$, for $\infty =$ `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$, as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$; `hIg` provides, for each line $\ell$, some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries $\infty$ to $\ell$ and for which $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$ is the preimage of $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$ under the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $\mathcal{F}$; `hIg_inj` says $\mathrm{OIg}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages of the $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $\mathrm{OIg}$. The supersingular group of hypotheses: `hSS_A` says $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular wherever the base-changed $q$-expansion $j$ of the classical modular invariant is regular (for every place $P$ of $\overline{F}_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ and, for each $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference between the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ is stable under preimage along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in \mathrm{OSS}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $\mathrm{OSS}(s)$ for every $a \in A$. Further, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\mathcal{F}$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (the same data as a constant reduction, without the place map), `hR` identifies `R.integers` with $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` says that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` if and only if its image in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$.
--
--   Arithmetic of the base. An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ is given. A field of small constants $k_0$ with $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is given together with $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`) and with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`). An auxiliary prime $\ell$ is given with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = qu$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $A_1$ the valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated with respect to the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathcal{F}$ obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathcal{F}$, and quantifies over the following further data.
--
--   First, over $k_0$-intermediate fields $F_0$ of $\mathcal{F}$ subject to four conditions: the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $\mathcal{F}$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of $\mathcal{F}$ whose underlying Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Second, writing $T_1$ for the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\mathcal{F}$ generated by the image of $K_1$, over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions, in the sense that the image in $\mathcal{F}$ of $a \in A_1$ agrees with the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathcal{F}$; over an element $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in $\mathcal{F}$ is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the base-changed $q$-expansion $j$ of the modular invariant, with $j_1 \ne 0$; and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $\jmath$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that (i) for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ in $\mathcal{F}$ lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is $\jmath$ of its $R_0$-residue, and (ii) $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ if and only if there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation ring of $s$ exactly when $\jmath(g)$ is in the valuation ring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   The model is $\mathfrak{X}_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and the two chart morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf`. Six abbreviations are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak{X}_1$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ there are elements $g, h$ of the corresponding chart algebra with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of $\mathcal{F}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation ring of $P$, has $P$-value in $A$, and that value has $A$-valuation $< 1$ precisely when `InMax x f`. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: $x$ maps to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ is a closed point (every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$); for every chart point $y$ over $x$ in either chart, every chart-algebra element whose image in $\mathcal{F}$ is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; and for every $y$ in the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. `Reads x Q`, for $Q$ a place of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, holds when every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has image in `R.integers` whose $R$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $Q$ and is a nonunit there exactly when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x` holds when for every line $\ell \ne \infty$ and every chart point $y$ over $x$, in either chart, there is a chart-algebra element outside $y$ whose image in $\mathcal{F}$ is a nonunit of $\mathrm{OIg}(\ell)$.
--
--   The assertion is then: for every $x \in \mathfrak{X}_1$ such that $x$ maps to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$, $x$ is a closed point, and, in both charts, every chart-algebra element whose image in $\mathcal{F}$ is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in every chart point over $x$, and for every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ and `Reads x Q`: for every point $y$ of the finite chart with `ιFin`-image $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not belong to `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   Thus the hypotheses on $x$ are the first four clauses of `GoodPt` and the conclusion is its fifth clause; the abbreviations `Centred` and `OffBranch` are introduced but do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the supersingularity-avoidance step on the Igusa leg of the semistable-covering construction, in the case $q = 2$: a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and reading a place outside the node set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ cannot lie over a supersingular $j$-invariant. It supplies the last clause of `GoodPt` for [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_two), the statement producing good points together with the off-branch and reading properties.
